30
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,850
GDP growth over the 11 years from 2014–15
has been 1.5% a year.

31
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,408
Do you know how much consumer prices have
risen? By 77%, according to Rosstat. I

32
00:02:57,408 --> 00:02:58,850
didn't make it up.

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,850
If you add it all up, that comes to about
7% inflation a year.

34
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,697
Most surprisingly, none of the basic
economic targets in the president's

35
00:03:09,697 --> 00:03:11,850
decrees since 2012 have been met.

36
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,836
For some reason the president doesn't
demand accountability or punish anyone.

37
00:03:16,836 --> 00:03:19,850
Everything stays the same. This cannot
continue.

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,397
Economic growth requires investment.
Unfortunately, the animation isn't working

39
00:03:26,397 --> 00:03:30,850
and the slide is obscured, but investment
is essential.

40
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:37,378
It also has to be effective. You can pay
to dig a hole and then pay again to fill

41
00:03:37,378 --> 00:03:37,850
it in.

42
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:44,347
How do we measure effectiveness? My
brother and I devised parameters to

43
00:03:44,347 --> 00:03:46,850
measure it across countries.

44
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:54,094
Capital investment: delta C is the
increase in investment. It can be

45
00:03:54,094 --> 00:03:57,850
calculated in percentages or rubles.

46
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:05,898
GDP growth over a period, such as a year,
can likewise be calculated in percentages

47
00:04:05,898 --> 00:04:06,850
or rubles.

48
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:15,659
The ratio of GDP growth to investment
growth, expressed as percentages, measures

49
00:04:15,659 --> 00:04:16,850
efficiency.

50
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,996
But there is also the opposite of
efficiency: inflation. What do those

51
00:04:21,996 --> 00:04:25,850
investments produce when we dig a hole and
fill it in?

52
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,850
Inflation. The growth of inflation
relative to the growth of investment.

53
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,034
These are the two parameters. One is
efficiency, like an energy efficiency

54
00:04:36,034 --> 00:04:36,850
coefficient.

55
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:43,874
The other is dissipation: energy lost in
the form of inflation, inflation growth

56
00:04:43,874 --> 00:04:45,850
relative to GDP growth.

57
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:54,850
Let's compare four countries. The smallest
rectangle is Russia.

58
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:02,000
It has the smallest increases in
investment and GDP. The slope of the red

59
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:07,850
line is the lowest: the lowest efficiency
of these countries.

60
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:15,850
The United States is higher, at 0.62.
Poland's efficiency is surprisingly high.

61
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:24,434
And look at China: the largest increase in
investment and the largest increase in

62
00:05:24,434 --> 00:05:24,850
GDP.

63
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:34,850
Now let's look at inflation. China is at
the bottom, the lowest at 0.27.

64
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:40,381
That's 0.27 inflation per 1% growth in
investment. Poland is higher than the

65
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:43,850
United States; Poland isn't better at
everything.

66
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,850
And look where our country is. Everything
goes down the drain.

67
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,850
Yes, we need to increase investment, but
everything goes down the drain.

68
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:01,159
We compared these coefficients, including
money-supply efficiency and GDP growth, in

69
00:06:01,159 --> 00:06:04,850
a kind of economic all-around ranking.

70
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:09,850
Of the fifty countries selected, we are in
fifty-first place.

71
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:15,941
Russia the great is in fifty-first place.
We are proud of our great souls and so on,

72
00:06:15,941 --> 00:06:17,850
yet we watch indifferently.

73
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,655
For 30 years. These efficiency measures
have been the same for the previous 15

74
00:06:24,655 --> 00:06:25,850
years and now.

75
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:31,446
Look at the industrial workforce. People
say things started improving when Putin

76
00:06:31,446 --> 00:06:34,850
